>> title: Mango Sticky Rice with Hedgehog-Cut Mango
>> servings: 2
>> time: 45 minutes
>> tags: exotic, watchme, fruit, dessert, knife-technique

Rinse @glutinous rice{1%cup} in a #sieve{} until the water runs mostly clear.

Cook rice with @water{1%cup} in a #rice cooker{} or covered #saucepan{} for ~{25%minutes}.

Warm @coconut milk{1%cup}, @sugar{3%tbsp}, and @kosher salt{1/4%tsp} in a #saucepan{} until dissolved.

Fold half the coconut sauce into the hot rice and rest covered for ~{10%minutes}.

-- watch: Mango cheek is sliced close to the flat pit without cutting through the skin.
Cut both cheeks from @ripe mango{1} with a #paring knife{}.

-- watch: Crosshatch cuts reach the peel but do not pierce it.
Score each mango cheek into a grid and turn it inside out.

Serve sticky rice with mango, remaining coconut sauce, and @toasted sesame seeds{1%tsp}.
